    detailedNotes: 'Acids and bases are two fundamental classes of chemical substances. Acids have a sour taste, turn blue litmus red, and have pH less than 7. Bases have a bitter taste and slippery feel, turn red litmus blue, and have pH greater than 7. Indicators are substances that change colour in acidic or basic solutions. Natural indicators include litmus (extracted from lichens), turmeric, and red cabbage juice. The pH scale ranges from 0 to 14, with 7 being neutral. Strong acids (pH 0-3) like HCl fully dissociate, while weak acids (pH 4-6) like acetic acid partially dissociate. Neutralisation is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water: Acid + Base → Salt + Water. This is an exothermic reaction.',
